          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness closes their shutters when they observe in the sky 12 to 15 glowing objects seemingly flying silently in formation. Observing a group of glowing objects crossing the sky in just a few minutes, on a weekend night, strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The movement is observed from North to South, which is consistent with the reported North-West to North wind in Bordeaux: weather. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
